            explanationEn: 'The insight of this chapter. Freud, Skinner, Rogers, all of them psychologists. All of them <strong>serious. But they differ not only in method, but in the basic conception of what a human being</strong> is. Is he driven by drives? Reinforcements? A search for meaning? Every approach is effective in certain situations, but there is no "single answer" that all psychologists agree on. This is not a weakness of the field, it is its nature.',
